    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "title",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "# Grocery store coverage targets"
      },
      {
        "id": "summary",
        "type": "markdown",
        "sourceId": "estimates",
        "body": "## Executive Summary\n\n**Use approximately 67,630 stores nationally as a rough planning target.** The summed state scenarios span 51,770\u201385,270; this is not a statistical interval.\n\n**Discovery remains partial.** 49 states have catalog record counts below even their lower planning scenarios.\n\n**Counts cannot certify accuracy.** AI selected a transparent estimation method using Census and SNAP aggregates. No extra paid model requests were made; store identity, open status and field accuracy still require evidence."
      },
      {
        "id": "scope",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Count physical groceries across chains and independents\n\nInclude general-line groceries, supermarkets, grocery supercenters and warehouse clubs. Exclude convenience stores, dollar stores, standalone pharmacies and specialist meat or produce shops. General merchandise stores with limited groceries and employer-free businesses are imperfectly covered by the anchors. Each row compares published canonical records with an estimate of physical stores; published records have not all been crawled or independently verified."
      },
      {
        "id": "findings",
        "type": "markdown",
        "sourceId": "estimates",
        "body": "## The active smaller-state cohort still needs broader discovery\n\nThe downloadable data retains both public-source counts; the table compares planning ranges and catalog counts. Ratios are record-count comparisons, not verified coverage. Low counts can indicate missing source discovery; high counts can indicate wider scope, duplication or undercounting in the public anchors. Review all three possibilities."
      },
      {
        "id": "cohort-chart",
        "type": "chart",
        "chartId": "cohort",
        "layout": "full"
      },
      {
        "id": "table",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "states",
        "layout": "full"
      },
      {
        "id": "iowa",
        "type": "markdown",
        "sourceId": "estimates",
        "body": "## Iowa is near the count target, with identity work still needed\n\nIowa has 735 catalog records against a rough target of 710 (590\u2013860 planning range). The underlying anchors are 709 Census establishments and 705 grocery-format SNAP records. Agreement at aggregate level is encouraging, but missing independent stores may be offset by duplicates, permanently closed stores or scope differences. Compare matched addresses and operating status before describing statewide coverage."
      },
      {
        "id": "next",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Use the targets to direct verification\n\n1. Prioritize states below the lower planning range for SNAP, OpenStreetMap, state inspection or licensing data and chain locator discovery.\n2. Report distinct in-scope operating stores, reviewed closures, unresolved identities and excluded formats separately.\n3. Check source overlap by address and coordinates, plus county and chain gaps; do not just compare totals.\n4. Continue phone, hours, timezone and provenance checks even when a count is near target. Targets do not change crawl limits, budgets, activation or acceptance gates."
      },
      {
        "id": "questions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## What could change the estimates?\n\nWhich current SNAP records are outside our scope? How many independent groceries do not accept SNAP or have employees? Which counties and chains have poor discovery? State licensing and inspection lists can help answer these questions, but some include restaurants or convenience stores and need filtering."
      },
      {
        "id": "caveats",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Caveats and assumptions\n\nCensus is a 2023 employer-establishment count downloaded October 21, 2026; SNAP aggregates were acquired October 20, 2026. Catalog counts are a fixed snapshot at 2026-10-21T05:22:47.531096+00:00, while the crawl continues. Census and SNAP have different definitions and overlap; they are not additive. The 2:1 weighting and 15%/20% buffers are AI-selected judgments, not validated growth rates or confidence bounds. All estimates have low confidence. The 50-state total excludes DC and territories. Never delete records, infer closure, claim exact missing-store counts or stop crawling solely because of these estimates."
      }
    ],
